<|channel>thought
<channel|>Your home energy dashboard is a powerful tool, but it comes with a hidden maintenance cost: data drift. 

While these tools are great for spotting high-drain appliances, they aren't "set-and-forget." Over time, smart meters and sensors require firmware updates or manual recalibration to stay accurate. If you don't monitor the hardware itself, you’ll waste mental energy troubleshooting "phantom" spikes that don't actually exist. Treat your dashboard like a digital appliance—it requires periodic upkeep to ensure the savings it promises are actually real. [end of text]


